IMPORT prelude

-- Control of Plants Act 1993 (Singapore) -- the licence and permit regime for importing and transhipping fresh fruits and
-- vegetables (ss 2, 7, 8), who needs a cultivation licence and when pesticides may be used (ss 9-11, 13), the five-year protection
-- of innovative pesticide data (ss 15, 16), prohibited plants (s 18), pest notices, land clearance and compensation (ss 21, 25,
-- 26), appeals (s 33), the penalty table (ss 7(4), 8(3), 21(6), (7), 25(3), 30(2), 34, 37(8), (9), 38(2)), protection from
-- liability (s 45) and composition (s 47).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CPA1993.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 25
-- of 2021 (s 8(5), wef 1 April 2022).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a grower, an importer of
-- produce, an exporter or a landowner actually meets. Not encoded: appointments and delegation (ss 3-6), the procurement-plan
-- inquiries on licensing (s 7(2), (3)), registration procedure (s 14), the certificate as evidence (s 19), quarantine (ss 22-24),
-- accredited agencies (s 27), export prohibitions (ss 28, 29) beyond the penalty, licence procedure (ss 31, 32) beyond the appeal,
-- investigation powers (s 37(1)-(7)), sampling and disposal (ss 39, 40), forfeiture, service, fees, exemptions and rules (ss 42-44,
-- 46, 48, 49). Nothing in the subsidiary legislation (prescribed residue levels, fees, compoundable offences) was read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Control of Plants Act 1993`

§§ `2, 7 -- who needs an import or transhipment licence`

-- s 2: "import" means to bring into Singapore "but does not include the bringing into Singapore ... (whether landed or transhipped
-- in Singapore) for the sole purpose of being carried to any other country". "tranship" means to bring a plant in and then (a) remove
-- it from the conveyance and (b) return it to the same conveyance or transfer it to another, for the purpose of export.
-- s 7(1): "A person must not import for sale, supply or distribution or tranship any fresh fruit or vegetable except under and in
-- accordance with the conditions of a licence issued by the Director-General." (4): $10,000 or 3 years or both.
--
-- "Fresh fruits and vegetables" are "unprocessed and raw fruits and vegetables which are intended for human consumption" (s 2).
-- Produce that never leaves its conveyance is neither imported nor transhipped (INFERENCE from the two definitions). Bringing in
-- produce for one's own use is an import, but not one "for sale, supply or distribution", so s 7 does not reach it (INFERENCE;
-- rules under s 49(2)(k) may).
DECLARE Movement IS ONE OF
    `import for sale`
    `import for supply or distribution`
    `import for own consumption`
    `transhipment`
    `transit without leaving the conveyance`

GIVEN `the movement` IS A Movement, `it is fresh produce for human consumption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a licence under s 7 is required` IF
    `it is fresh produce for human consumption` AND
        CONSIDER `the movement`
        WHEN `import for sale` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `import for supply or distribution` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `transhipment` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the movement` IS A Movement, `it is fresh produce for human consumption` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the movement is an offence under s 7` IF
    `a licence under s 7 is required` `the movement` `it is fresh produce for human consumption` AND (NOT `holds a licence`)

§§ `8 -- the per-consignment permit and the due diligence defence`

-- s 8(1): a licensee must not import fresh produce for sale, supply or distribution unless (a) it has a permit "in respect of each
-- consignment" and imports in accordance with it; (b) "the whole consignment" conforms to the permit's description; (c) the whole
-- consignment contains no prohibited pesticide residue, nor pesticide or toxic chemical residue above the prescribed levels; (d) it
-- meets any prescribed sanitary standards; (e) the licensee gives "satisfactory evidence" of (c) and (d); and (f) each container
-- bears "the producer's name and address" and other prescribed particulars. (2): transhipment needs a permit per consignment too.
-- (3): $10,000 or 3 years or both.
DECLARE Consignment HAS
    `has a permit for this consignment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conforms to the permit description` IS A BOOLEAN
    `free of prohibited pesticide residue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `residues within prescribed levels` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets sanitary standards` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfactory evidence given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `containers bear producer name and address` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the consignment` IS A Consignment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the import complies with s 8(1)` IF
        `the consignment`'s `has a permit for this consignment`
    AND `the consignment`'s `conforms to the permit description`
    AND `the consignment`'s `free of prohibited pesticide residue`
    AND `the consignment`'s `residues within prescribed levels`
    AND `the consignment`'s `meets sanitary standards`
    AND `the consignment`'s `satisfactory evidence given`
    AND `the consignment`'s `containers bear producer name and address`

-- s 8(4): a defence for the person charged to prove (a) the offence "was due to the act or default of another person or some other
-- cause beyond A's control"; AND (b) A "took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence". (5): if the defence blames
-- another person, A may not rely on it, without the court's permission, unless "within a period ending 7 clear days before the
-- hearing" A served on the prosecutor a written notice identifying that person.
DECLARE Defence HAS
    `due to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `due to another cause beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `clear days before hearing notice was served` IS A NUMBER
    `notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the defence` IS A Defence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 8(4) defence is made out` IF
        (`the defence`'s `due to another person` OR `the defence`'s `due to another cause beyond control`)
    AND `the defence`'s `took all reasonable precautions`
    AND (    (NOT `the defence`'s `due to another person`)
          OR `the defence`'s `court gave permission`
          OR (`the defence`'s `notice was served` AND `the defence`'s `clear days before hearing notice was served` >= 7)
          OR `the defence`'s `due to another cause beyond control`)

GIVEN `the consignment` IS A Consignment, `the defence` IS A Defence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee is guilty under s 8(3)` IF
    (NOT `the import complies with s 8(1)` `the consignment`) AND (NOT `the s 8(4) defence is made out` `the defence`)

§§ `9, 10, 11 -- cultivation licence and pesticide use`

-- s 9: "This Part does not apply to (a) the cultivation of any plant for domestic and home gardening purposes; and (b) the
-- cultivation of any plant which is not for sale."
-- s 10: "A person must not cultivate any plant on any premises except under and in accordance with a licence".
-- s 11(1): no pesticide in cultivation unless (a) "the pesticide is registered with the Director-General" and (b) the person is a
-- certified pesticide operator "or the use is supervised by a certified pesticide operator". (2): storage, container disposal and
-- residue levels as prescribed. s 34(a): contravening s 10 or 11(1) and (2) is an offence, $10,000 or 3 years or both.
--
-- Because s 9 disapplies the whole Part, the pesticide rules in s 11 bind only cultivation for sale.
GIVEN `for home gardening` IS A BOOLEAN, `for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 3 applies` IF (NOT `for home gardening`) AND `for sale`

GIVEN `for home gardening` IS A BOOLEAN, `for sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cultivating is an offence under s 10` IF `Part 3 applies` `for home gardening` `for sale` AND (NOT `licensed`)

GIVEN `for home gardening` IS A BOOLEAN, `for sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `pesticide registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `user certified` IS A BOOLEAN, `supervised by a certified operator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pesticide use breaches s 11(1)` IF
        `Part 3 applies` `for home gardening` `for sale`
    AND (    (NOT `pesticide registered`)
          OR ((NOT `user certified`) AND (NOT `supervised by a certified operator`)))

-- s 13: the Director-General may suspend or cancel a certification if the operator (a) uses or supervises an unregistered
-- pesticide; (b) uses one "otherwise than in accordance with the instructions specified by the manufacturer"; (c) fails to store as
-- prescribed; (d) disposes of a container otherwise than as prescribed; or (e) fails to keep required records.
DECLARE OperatorConduct IS ONE OF
    `used an unregistered pesticide`
    `ignored the manufacturer's instructions`
    `stored a pesticide improperly`
    `disposed of a container improperly`
    `kept no records of use`
    `was convicted of an unrelated traffic offence`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A OperatorConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `certification may be suspended or cancelled` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `was convicted of an unrelated traffic offence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `15, 16 -- protection of innovative pesticide data`

-- s 15(1): for confidential supporting information in an "innovative pesticide application", during the protected period the
-- Director-General must keep it confidential and "must not use" it to decide any other application. (2): "protected period" is "a
-- period of 5 years from the date the innovative pesticide application is or was ... received"; an innovative application is one
-- made after 8 January 1999 naming an active ingredient not mentioned in any earlier application.
-- s 16(1): despite that, it may be disclosed or used (a)(i) with the applicant's consent or (ii) if "necessary to protect the
-- health or safety of members of the public".
GIVEN `years since the application was received` IS A NUMBER, `active ingredient is new` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `applicant consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `necessary for public health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the data may be used for another application` IF
        (NOT `active ingredient is new`)
    OR  `years since the application was received` >= 5
    OR  `applicant consents`
    OR  `necessary for public health or safety`

§§ `18 -- prohibited plants found on land`

-- s 18: if a prohibited plant is found growing in contravention of a s 17 order, "the owner and the occupier of the land are deemed
-- to have permitted the plant to grow unless" the owner or occupier proves (a) it was planted "without the owner's or the occupier's
-- knowledge and consent"; AND (b) on becoming aware of it they "forthwith effectually eradicated and destroyed it".
GIVEN `planted without knowledge and consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `eradicated forthwith on becoming aware` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is deemed to have permitted it` IF
    (NOT `planted without knowledge and consent`) OR (NOT `eradicated forthwith on becoming aware`)

§§ `21, 25, 26 -- pest notices, clearing land, compensation`

-- s 21(1), (2): an authorised officer may enter land to look for pests upon serving written notice on the owner or occupier "at
-- least 6 hours before the time of intended entry".
GIVEN `written notice served` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entry under s 21(1) is on proper notice` IF `written notice served` AND `hours of notice` >= 6

-- s 21(7): an owner or occupier who "wilfully fails" to comply with a s 21(3) notice -- $10,000 or 3 years or both "and, in the case
-- of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction".
-- s 25(3): an owner or occupier who "fails to comply" with a notice to clear land -- the same, but "$500 for every day". s 25 has
-- no "wilfully".
GIVEN `wilful` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing a s 21(3) pest notice is an offence` IF `wilful` AND (NOT `complied in time`)

GIVEN `wilful` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing a s 25(1) clearance notice is an offence` IF NOT `complied in time`

-- s 26: where cultivation is destroyed under a s 25(1) notice the Minister "may, in his or her discretion" pay compensation, but
-- (a) "no compensation is to be paid for any diseased plant"; (b) value is market value at destruction, the Director-General's
-- decision on it final; (c) it may be withheld or reduced for non-compliance with a notice or neglect contributing to the pest.
GIVEN `destroyed under a s 25 notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the plant was diseased` IS A BOOLEAN, `market value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most compensation that may be paid` IS
    IF `destroyed under a s 25 notice` AND (NOT `the plant was diseased`)
    THEN `market value`
    ELSE 0

§§ `33 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 33(1): a person aggrieved by a refusal to issue or renew, or a suspension or revocation, "may, within 7 days of the receipt of
-- the notice ... appeal in writing to the Minister whose decision is final". (2): a suspension or revocation takes effect despite a
-- pending appeal "unless the Minister otherwise orders".
-- Counting day 7 as within time is an INFERENCE; the Act does not say how the 7 days are reckoned.
GIVEN `days since notice received` IS A NUMBER, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF `in writing` AND `days since notice received` <= 7

GIVEN `appeal pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revocation has effect meanwhile` IF NOT `Minister ordered otherwise`

§§ `Penalty table`

-- Every offence the Act creates carries a fine not exceeding $10,000. Imprisonment is up to 3 years for each, except s 37(9)
-- (altering or destroying required documents, false or misleading statements, failing a lawful demand): "12 months".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 7 unlicensed import or transhipment`
    `s 8 importing outside the permit`
    `s 21(6) obstructing entry to look for pests`
    `s 21(7) wilfully ignoring a pest notice`
    `s 25(3) ignoring a clearance notice`
    `s 30(2) falsifying a phytosanitary certificate`
    `s 34 unlicensed cultivation or pesticide breach`
    `s 34 breaching a prohibition order`
    `s 37(8) obstructing an authorised officer`
    `s 37(9) false statement to an authorised officer`
    `s 38(2) removing an identification label`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 37(9) false statement to an authorised officer` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 36

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the daily fine after conviction` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 21(7) wilfully ignoring a pest notice` THEN 100
    WHEN `s 25(3) ignoring a clearance notice` THEN 500
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS 10000 + `the daily fine after conviction` `the offence` * `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `45, 47 -- protection from liability and composition`

-- s 45: no suit lies against the Director-General or an authorised officer for anything done in the discharge of their duties
-- "unless the thing was done or omitted to be done in bad faith".
GIVEN `in discharge of duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a suit lies against the officer` IF (NOT `in discharge of duties`) OR `in bad faith`

-- s 47(1): the Director-General may compound an offence "which is prescribed as an offence which may be compounded" by collecting
-- "a sum not exceeding $1,000". (3): on composition, any article seized "must be forfeited to the Board".
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is within power` IF `prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` <= 1000
